+Brief economics: a subagent's cost is driven by how many tool calls it makes, because
+every call re-reads its whole context. A brief that already contains everything lets it
+finish in a few calls. So paste what it needs verbatim (its spec section, helper
+signatures, small files it edits, a test-style example) instead of pointing at paths.
+Keep each brief under ~1,500 words; a chunk that needs more is too big or too coupled
+to delegate.
 
